    <h2>📌 Principle</h2>
    <p>Sustainability</p>
    <h2>❓ What</h2>
    <p>Have enough people to support your product: tired employees result in "revolving door", loss of knowledge, and as a result - lower quality. Be ready for spikes in demand, both sudden and planned. Be even more ready for outages and have procedures to minimize downtimes. If an issue occurs, fix it in a way that will minimize or remove the possibility of recurrence. Most importantly, remember: slow and steady wins the race.</p>
    <h2>🪙 Business impact</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Agents' fatigue</li>
        <li>Inaccessible product</li>
        <li>Recurring issues</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>❌ Poor implementation</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Drains mental capacity of support agents reducing quality investigation quality.</li>
        <li>Wastes time by forcing to fix the same issues again and again.</li>
        <li>Promotes unrealistic expectations of explosive scaling.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>✅ Good implementation</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Keeps agents' minds fresh and ready for challenges.</li>
        <li>Minimizes user impact during downtimes.</li>
        <li>Encourages product preservation.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>🪢 Alignment</h2>
    <p>Workforce Planning and SRE On-call fatigue</p>
